    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"pipeline - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\":\n    \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/pipeline.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [pipeline()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-function}\n    | EdgeCase\n  description: A water supply network, with pipe capacities and costs.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [pipeline()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-function}\n    | EdgeCase\n  description: A water supply network, with pipe capacities and costs.\ntitle: >-\n  [pipeline()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-function}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: A water supply network, with pipe capacities and costs.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nA water supply network, with pipe capacities and costs.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/example_networks.py#L503-L578){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\npipeline()\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\nThe water system of a made-up city: water flows from a reservoir through two intakes and\ntwo treatment plants, across a valley, and into the city's two districts. Each edge is a\npipe with a capacity (the most water it can carry a day) and a cost per unit of water, so\nit's the example for flows and cuts: how much water can reach the city, which pipes limit\nit, and the cheapest way to deliver a given amount.\n\nNetwork Properties:\n\n- 11 nodes (facilities, labeled by name), with the source `\"Reservoir\"` and the sink\n  `\"City\"`\n- 14 edges (pipes, in the direction the water flows)\n- Directed, unweighted (capacities and costs are attributes)\n\nNode Attributes:\n\n- `kind`: `\"source\"`, `\"intake\"`, `\"pump\"`, `\"plant\"`, `\"junction\"`, `\"tank\"`,\n  `\"district\"` or `\"sink\"`\n- `pos`: an `(x, y)` position for a schematic drawing, from the reservoir on the left to the\n  city on the right\n\nEdge Attributes:\n\n- `capacity`: the most the pipe can carry, in megaliters (ML) a day\n- `cost`: the cost of moving one megaliter through the pipe (pumping and treatment)\n\nThe flow methods read the `capacity` attribute, and `minimum_cost_flow()` the `cost`\nattribute, without being told.\n\nWhat to Look For:\n\n- **A bottleneck across the valley.** At most 45 ML a day reaches the city, however the\n  water is routed: the two pipes across the valley, West Plant to Valley Junction (25) and\n  East Plant to Ridge Tank (20), form the minimum cut. Everything upstream could carry\n  more.\n- **Cheap and narrow, or wide and costly.** The East Plant is fed by an old gravity\n  aqueduct (10 ML a day at a cost of 1) and by the Hill Pump (30 ML a day at a cost of 3\n  per pipe). The cheapest way to deliver 40 ML a day uses no pumping; only the last 5 of\n  the 45 ML need the pump.\n- **Rising marginal cost.** Delivering 10 ML a day costs 50, 35 ML costs 200, 40 ML costs\n  235 and 45 ML costs 285, as ever more expensive routes come into use.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The pipeline network.\n:::\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nDraw the network as a schematic, from the reservoir to the city:\n\n::: {#7449d2cd .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\npipeline = ec.pipeline()\n\npipeline.plot(layout=\"pos\", color_by=\"kind\", label_by=\"label\", width=700, height=360)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}</style><div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\n<style>.ec-plot > svg { display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; }</style>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"700\" height=\"360\" viewBox